dict(id='KWG-03',severity='major',kind='dangling field semantics',items=['KERNEL-0094','KERNEL-0037','KERNEL-0038'],claim="KernelTx.expect: Invariant[] and KernelTx.onFail: 'reject'|'repair'|'downgrade' are declared but nothing in the base or volumes says who sets them (StageDecl.invariants, §4.1, is the likely producer), which op checks expect, or what each onFail value does; E_BELOW_MIN_AREA / E_BELOW_MIN_WIDTH ('a class floor declared by the caller') have no named producing op (no op signature takes a floor except absorbSliver, which absorbs instead of failing).",link='§3.3: define expect (filled from StageDecl.invariants / the caller class floors; checked at commit on the touched faces, returning E_BELOW_MIN_AREA/WIDTH/ANGLE) and the three onFail values (reject: return the code; repair: run §5 local repair on the overlay; downgrade: the stage ladder rung), each with its consumer in §5.1-§5.2.'),
